        "rows": [
          "| `perps.position_opened` | A fill opened a perps position from flat (every dex, builder dexes as `dex:COIN`) | `schema` (`candle.perps.position_event/1`), `event`, `network`, `address`, `coin`, `dex`, `side`, `dir`, `size`, `price`, `startPosition`, `closedPnl`, `fee`, `fillId`, `hash`, `fillTime`, `source` |",
          "| `perps.position_closed` | A fill took a perps position to zero | as `perps.position_opened` |",
          "| `perps.liquidated` | A fill liquidated your wallet's position | as `perps.position_opened`, plus `liquidation: { markPx, method }` |"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "docs-webhooks-lateness",
      "scenario": "docs",
      "args": {
        "file": "apps/docs/src/content/docs/developers/webhooks.md"
      },
      "outcome": {
        "text": "The three `perps.position_*` / `perps.liquidated` events are read from the perps ingest, not streamed: they can arrive up to about two hours after `fillTime`, and one fill emits at most once (a re-ingest sends nothing new). Real-time critical-risk alerts come from `perps.risk_critical`, which needs the risk monitor. They cover every EVM TEE wallet the ingest reads, including those of private and unlisted agents; the public board still shows only public agents."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "sdk-changelog-entry",
      "scenario": "docs",
      "args": {
        "file": "packages/sdk/CHANGELOG.md"
      },
      "outcome": {
        "text": "Release 0.6.26 (BE-3758), with CLI 0.13.32 and MCP 0.10.37; this release also publishes the unreleased BE-3767 fields below. `perpsOverviewActivity(walletId)` (type `PerpsOverviewActivity`): one EVM TEE wallet's open Hyperliquid orders across the default and every builder-deployed perp dex (each row tagged with its `dex`) and its bound key's withdrawals in flight; needs `account:read`, and either list is null when its read failed. `@candledottv/agent-sdk/webhooks` adds the typed perps position events `perps.position_opened`, `perps.position_closed` and `perps.liquidated` (`candle.perps.position_event/1`, with `fillTime`). MCP adds `candle_perps_activity`; the CLI adds `candle perps activity` and `candle perps thresholds --key <prefix|label>` (the owner's read of a key's stored thresholds and perps limits, with the device token)."
      }
    },
